  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Mulliganed a one-land 6-card hand down to 5 cards. While the hand was risky with only one Mountain and needing blue sources, it had a reasonable curve (2-drop, 3-drop mana rock that fixes colors) and going to 5 cards in Limited is extremely punishing. The Mana Geode in particular would help fix the mana if they could reach 3 mana total.",
      "action_taken": "Chose to mulligan to 5 cards",
      "better_line": "Keep the 6-card hand. One land with a mana rock is risky but playable, especially since going to 5 severely reduces the chances of having a functional hand. Drawing any land in the first two turns (likely ~60%+) makes this hand serviceable.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 4,
      "player": "Sonnet Vet",
      "decision_index": 4,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Passed with 1 untapped Swamp and no other possible plays. The only available action was activating Scroll of Avacyn ({1}, sacrifice: draw a card), which would have converted an otherwise wasted mana into a card. There's no reason to save the Scroll - they don't control an Angel and are unlikely to get one, and the 1 mana has no other use this turn.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, wasting 1 mana and missing a free card draw.",
      "better_line": "Activate Scroll of Avacyn to draw a card, since there's no other use for the mana this turn and the Scroll's value doesn't meaningfully increase by waiting.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 33,
      "player": "GPT53C Stoic",
      "decision_index": 15,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Player passed in postcombat main with 1 untapped Swamp and Scroll of Avacyn available to activate. There is nothing else to spend the mana on this turn, so activating Scroll to draw a card is free value. Waiting gains nothing — the Scroll has no battlefield synergies and the mana would go to waste.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, ending the turn with 1 unused mana and Scroll of Avacyn still on the battlefield.",
      "better_line": "Activate Scroll of Avacyn (pay {1} with the untapped Swamp, sacrifice it, draw a card) to gain a free card draw with mana that would otherwise be wasted.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 37,
      "player": "GPT53C Stoic",
      "decision_index": 17,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Sacrificed Scroll of Avacyn without an Angel in play, missing the 5 life bonus. Baneslayer Angel is in hand and could potentially be cast in a few turns, at which point Scroll would provide draw + 5 life instead of just draw.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Scroll of Avacyn immediately for just a card draw without the Angel bonus.",
      "better_line": "Hold Scroll of Avacyn until Baneslayer Angel is on the battlefield to gain the additional 5 life. The extra card draw now is less valuable than 5 life later, especially since the player is at 20 life and not under immediate pressure.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 52,
      "player": "GPT53C Stoic",
      "decision_index": 22,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Mistwalker 1/4 could block the attacking Wakedancer 2/2 with no risk — Mistwalker survives at 1/2 remaining toughness, prevents 2 damage to the player, and deals 1 damage to the Wakedancer. There's essentially no downside to blocking.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to block, taking 2 damage for free.",
      "better_line": "Block the Wakedancer 2/2 with Mistwalker 1/4. Mistwalker survives the combat (4 toughness vs 2 power), prevents 2 player damage, and deals 1 damage to the Wakedancer.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 99,
      "player": "Sonnet Vet",
      "decision_index": 34,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Failed to block Mistwalker (1/4 flying) with Reaper from the Abyss (6/6 flying). Blocking would have killed Mistwalker for free (Reaper survives at 6/5) and triggered Morbid at end step to potentially destroy another opponent creature. Instead, took 1 unnecessary damage and missed both the creature trade and Morbid trigger.",
      "action_taken": "No response (timed out), did not assign Reaper from the Abyss as blocker",
      "better_line": "Block Mistwalker with Reaper from the Abyss to kill it for free and enable Morbid trigger at end step",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 121,
      "player": "GPT53C Stoic",
      "decision_index": 39,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Missed a line to kill Reaper from the Abyss (6/6). By casting Magma Jet on Reaper during combat (2 damage) and activating Mistwalker once to make it 2/3 (dealing 2 combat damage), Reaper would have 4 damage marked. Then post-combat, Spitting Earth with 3 Mountains deals 3 more damage (total 7), killing the 6-toughness Reaper. Instead, Mistwalker dies for nothing and Reaper survives.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority during combat, letting Mistwalker deal only 1 damage to Reaper before dying.",
      "better_line": "Cast Magma Jet targeting Reaper from the Abyss (2 damage), activate Mistwalker ({1}{U}: +1/-1 making it 2/3) to deal 2 combat damage to Reaper (4 total), then post-combat cast Spitting Earth on Reaper for 3 damage (7 total), destroying it.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 123,
      "player": "Sonnet Vet",
      "decision_index": 41,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Passed the turn with 4 untapped mana and useful spells available. Magma Jet could kill Wakedancer (removing a 2/2 attacker) and Scry 2 to dig for answers to Reaper from the Abyss. Since Sonnet Vet controls no creatures, Reaper's morbid trigger from the Wakedancer death would have no valid target on their side. Passing wastes the opportunity to remove an attacker and dig for critical answers.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority in postcombat main phase, ending the turn without casting any spells.",
      "better_line": "Cast Magma Jet targeting Wakedancer to kill it and Scry 2 to dig for answers to Reaper from the Abyss (such as Angelic Edict or Pirated Copy setup). Reaper's morbid would have no legal target on Sonnet Vet's side.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 127,
      "player": "Sonnet Vet",
      "decision_index": 42,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "With Reaper from the Abyss threatening to dominate the game and no creatures or removal in hand that can deal with it, the Scry 2 from Magma Jet could help find critical answers. Sonnet Vet has no board presence and needs to dig for solutions urgently. While saving Magma Jet for later has some merit (e.g., combining with Spitting Earth for 5 damage, or killing an activated Guardian Idol), the Scry 2 to find answers to the 6/6 flier is very valuable when behind.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without casting Magma Jet",
